Standard Exercism alphametics. Implement Solve: parse the puzzle, split on "==", split addends on "+", build the coefficient of each letter (sum of addends minus the result), and do backtracking over the letters.

Key points:
- Return value type is map[string]int, keys are single-character strings.
- If no solution exists, return an error.
- Leading zeros are not allowed for multi-digit words.
- The last test case has 199 addends and 10 letters — with backtracking it's 10! = 3.6 million permutations, and each check is O(1) via coefficients. No problem.

